From 4eee7dddc32fab350dd12ef88dfbc7c502642525 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 15:39:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/33] ASoC: qcom: add msm8998 machine driver

Adds the ASoC machine driver for Qualcomm MSM8998 / APQ8098, used for
audio on the Google Pixel 2 XL (taimen).

6.18 mainline dropped the entire msm8998 ASoC machine-driver family
(SND_SOC_MSM8998 and its SND_SOC_LPASS_MSM8998 platform driver) that
existed at this port's 6.0 base. lpass-msm8998.c is brought back
unmodified alongside the machine driver, since msm8998.c hard-selects
SND_SOC_LPASS_MSM8998 and there is nothing to reconcile in the
platform driver itself -- it is the same LPASS CPU DAI/platform glue
every other Qualcomm SoC in this directory has.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
